F INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.  211 \nANSWERED ON 2ND FEBRUARY, 2017 \n \nIMPROVEMENT OF ROAD INFRASTRUCTURE IN HILLY AREAS \n \n211. SHRI KUNWAR PUSHPENDRA SINGH CHANDEL: \n \nWill the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS  \n \n������������������������������\nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has taken/ proposes to take any initiative to improve road infrastructure \nto promote pilgrimage tourism in hilly areas;  \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof including the funds earmarked/allocated/spent during each of the last \nthree years;  \n \n(c) whether the Government proposes to construct/widen all National Highways in Himalayan/trans -\nHimalayan region; and  \n \n(d) if so, the details thereof including the funds earmarked/allocated/spent during each of the last \nthree years?  \n \nANSWER \n�\nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n(SHRI PON RADHAKRISHNAN) \n \n(a) to (d)The Ministry is primarily responsible for development and maintenance of National \nHighways (NHs)  network in India through its implementing agencies like National Highways \nAuthority of India ( NHAI), Border Roads Organization  (BRO), National Highways and \nInfrastructure Development Co rporation Limited (NHIDCL) and respective State PWDs.  The \ndevelopment and maintenance of NHs is a continuous process. The works on NHs, including the NHs \nin hilly States  to promote pilgrimage tourism , are accordingly taken up as per available resources, \ninter-se priority and traffic density to keep the NHs in traffic worthy conditions.  \n \nThe Ministry has taken up detailed review of NHs network with a view to develop the road \nconnectivity to Border areas and hilly States including connectivity Improvement Program for Char -\nDham (Kedarnath, Badrinath, Yamunothri & Gangot ri in Uttarakhand) etc . The details of the funds \nearmarked/allocated/spent during each of the last three years State wise is at Annexure. \n  \n\nANNEXURE \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY  TO PARTS (a) TO (d)  OF LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION N O. 211 FOR ANSWER ON  02.02.2017 ASKED BY SHRI \nKUMWAR PUSHPENDRA SINGH CHANDEL R EGARDING IMROVEMENT OF ROAD \nINFRASTRUCTURE IN HILLY AREAS  \nThe State /UT-wise details of funds allocated/utilized for development of NHs during each of the \nlast three years     \n                                                                                                                        (Amount in Rs. crore) \n�\nSl. \nNo. States/UTs/Schemes/Agency 2013-14 2014-15 2015-16 \nAlloc. Expd. Alloc. Expd. Alloc. Expd. \n1 Andhra Pradesh 188.04 187.62 221.45 221.45 1,039.42 1,000.43 \n2 Arunachal Pradesh 1.09 1.09 0.50 0.50 2.40 1.83 \n3 Assam 205.10 199.41 141.76 141.76 78.79 78.09 \n4 Bihar 304.57 271.33 276.65 276.65 706.92 707.86 \n5 Chhattisgarh 43.35 25.29 71.25 71.25 359.94 339.80 \n6 Goa 20.66 20.66 17.72 17.72 120.00 119.98 \n7 Gujarat 146.54 140.91 206.96 206.96 228.60 225.77 \n8 Haryana 53.51 53.51 60.48 60.48 90.00 89.85 \n9 Himachal Pradesh 100.44 99.74 134.57 134.57 140.00 139.96 \n10 Jammu & Kashmir 0.00 0.00 0.00 0.00 25.00 22.86 \n11 Jharkhand 70.32 70.32 63.83 63.83 35.00 38.08 \n12 Karnataka 165.85 164.55 269.72 269.72 633.43 639.55 \n13 Kerala 272.73 258.84 67.18 67.18 132.24 137.65 \n14 Madhya Pradesh 155.01 150.67 239.23 239.23 937.76 928.29 \n15 Maharashtra 177.23 177.01 190.04 190.04 431.20 423.28 \n16 Manipur 54.72 54.39 32.60 32.60 40.00 40.00 \n17 Meghalaya 35.70 33.61 43.30 43.30 15.00 15.00 \n18 Mizoram 22.11 20.57 39.53 39.53 35.00 28.50 \n19 Nagaland 44.65 44.65 46.20 46.20 50.00 46.27 \n26 Tripura 0.00 0.00 0.00 0.00 5.00 0.00 \n27 Uttar Pradesh 284.14 284.14 493.81 493.81 1,530.34 1,527.74 \n28 Uttarakhand 87.84 85.90 169.51 169.51 245.92 245.69 \n29 West Bengal 134.10 134.10 283.61 283.61 808.95 811.98 \n30 Andaman & Nicobar Islands 0.00 0.00 14.61 14.61 2.00 1.53 \n31 Chandigarh 0.00 0.00 4.95 4.95 1.00 0.00 \n3