side Dr. KSSR) \n \n \nRs. 200/- per hour  \n (inside Dr. KSSR) \nRs. 2000/- per hour \n(outside Dr. KSSR) \n \nRs. 100/- per hour  for \ndry practice only. \n (inside Dr. KSSR) \nRs. 2000/- per hour \n(outside Dr. KSSR) \n \nRs. 10/- per hour  \n (inside Dr. KSSR) \nRs. 100/- per ho"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|11|STARRED   |86", "t": "Reforms in Public Broadcasting", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF INFORMATION AND BROADCASTING \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 86  \n(TO BE ANSWERED ON 08.2.2017) \n  \n \nREFORMS IN PUBLIC BROADCASTING  \n \n*86. SHRI CH. MALLA REDDY: \n      SHRI MUTHAMSETTI SRINIVASA RAO (AVANTHI): \n \nWill the MINISTER OF INFORMATION AND BROADCASTING be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether several committees, including Sam Pitroda Panel have recommended structural \nreforms in the Public Broadcasting and if so, the details thereof;  \n \n(b) whether a panel of Secretaries has also suggested the Government to make public \nbroadcasters, Doordarshan (DD) and All India Radio (AIR), corporate entities so as to \nreduce their dependence on Government funds and give them elbow room to take \ndecisions; and  \n \n(c)   if so, the reaction of the Government thereto? \n \n \nANSWER  \n \nTHE MINISTER OF INFORMATION AND BROADCASTING                                      \n[SHRI M. VENKAIAH NAIDU] \n \n(a) to (c): A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n  \n  \n\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO  IN REPLY TO PARTS ( a) TO ( c) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 86 FOR ANSWER ON 08.2.2017. \n(a): In the recent past, the Government had set up an Expert Committee under the \nChairmanship of Shri Sam Pitroda on 28.01.2013, to review the functioning of Prasar Bharati. \nThe Committee had submitted its Report on 24.1.2014 and recommended framing a long-term \nvision and strategy for Prasar Bharati that would include and be dependent upon the \ntechnology choices, ass essment of human resources, review of programming, including \nreview of existing channels and also a study of independent sources of finances for Prasar \nBharati. Details of recommendations of the Expert Committee may be seen in its Report \nwhich is available  on the website of the Ministry of Information and Broadcasting at the \nfollowing address: www.mib.nic.in>>Documents>>Broadcasting-Documents>>Report of \nExpert Committee on Prasar Bharati Vol 1 and Report of Expert Committee on Prasar \nBharati Vol 2. \n(b):  A Group of Secretaries has been considering, apart from issues relating to other \nMinistries, the issues concerning the Ministry of Information and Broadcasting also but no \nReport of the Group has been received by this Ministry. \n(c):   In view of (b) above, the question does not arise. \n \n***** \n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|11|STARRED   |87", "t": "IT Policy", "head": "Government of India \nMinistry of Drinking Water and Sanitation \n  \n����������\n���������������������� 87 �\n������������������ 02-02-2017 \nClean Toilets \n \n†87. SHRI SADASHIV LOKHANDE: \n�\n��������������������  DRINKING WATER AND SANITATION ������������������� : \n�\n�������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������� \n���������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������� \n������������\n�\n������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������ \n��������������������������������������������������������������������\n�\n������������������������������������\n�\n����������������������������������������������������������������\n�\nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF DRINKING WATER & \nSANITATION \n(SHRI RAMESH CHANDAPPA JIGAJINAGI) \n \n \n����� ���� ��������� ��� ��������� ������ ���� ����������� ������ ������ ���� ����������� ��� ���� ������ \n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������� \n������������������������������������������������������\n�\n������������