5190  4883 \nKarnataka  194  195  196 116094 114608 112591 89690  82337\nKerala  168  172  174  72834  72280  71619  46787  45350 \nMadhya Pradesh  230  223  217  120152  114926  109279  57210  54267 \nMaharashtra  383  379  375 182929 177146 167652 104728  98523\nManipur  1  1  1  115  115  115  115  115 \nMeghalaya  1  1  1  480  480  420  257  159 \nNagaland  1  1  1 240 240 240 63  86\nOdisha  99  99  97  52182  51342  49949  18084  18966 \nPuducherry  18  18  18  9834  9768  9751  4788  4342 \nPunjab  113  111  105 53895 52053 47842 21382  18334\nRajasthan  143  139  131  71800  66786  61431  28909  26735 \nSikkim  1  1  1  894  894  834  623  431 \nTamil Nadu  534  535  528 327269 320362 311964 178537  171283\nTelangana  331  313  291 230782 192922 172580 103253  84706\nTripura  2  4  3  600  762  702  308  481 \nUttar Pradesh  307  306  299 159296 156207 147712 75542  66370\nUttarakhand  34  35  32 14732 14612 13454 5526  5868\nWest Bengal  91  93  95  43144  42808  41544  21577  22191 \nGrand Total  3455  3430  3352  1904922  1822932  1732603  981436  915196 "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|11|UNSTARRED |555", "t": "Unnat Bharat Programme", "head": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK  SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.555 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 12.04.2017 \n \nINTEGRAL COACH FACTORY \n \n \n*555. SHRIMATI  V. SATHYA BAMA: \n          \n Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state : \n \n(a) the steps taken by the Gov ernment to provide autonomy to the \nIntegral Coach Factory (ICF), Chennai and also additional funds to \nICF for the development of state-of-the-art technology coaches; and \n \n(b) the total manufacturing capacity of ICF and the steps taken by the \nGovernment to improve exports of rail coaches from India? \n \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS \n(SHRI SURESH PRABHAKAR PRABHU) \n \n(a)  & (b)   A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n***** \n \n\nSTATEMENT  REFERRED  TO  IN  REPLY  TO  PARTS   (a)  AND  (b)  OF  \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 555 BY SHRIMATI V. SATHYA BAMA TO BE \nANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 12.04.2017 REGARDING INTEGRAL \nCOACH FACTORY \n \n(a) At present, there is no proposal to give autonomy to Integral Coach \nFactory, Chennai (ICF). However, General Managers have been \ndelegated full powers  for accepting all works and stores tenders. \nDevelopment of technology is a continuous process e.g. new design of \n Linke Hofmann Busch (LHB) coaches having higher speed potential, \nbetter riding comfort and improved safety features has been introduced \nin Indian Railways. An outlay of  ` 199.8 crore has been provided in the \nyear 2017-18 for the work of modernization for complete switch over to \nLHB coach manufacturing at Integral Coach Factory (ICF), Chennai. Also, \ntwo Semi High Speed Multiple Unit Train sets with quicker acceleration \nand contemporary passenger amenities like on board infotainment and \nPassenger Information System, Automatic Doors with retractable coach \nfootsteps and Zero Discharge Vacuum based Bio -toilets etc. have been \nincluded in Production P rogram for 2017 -18 for Integral Coach Factory \n(ICF), Chennai. \n(b) The present manufacturing capacity of ICF is 1700 coaches per \nannum.  To encourage the export of Rolling Stock including rail coaches, \npowers have been delegated to General Managers of Productio n Units of \nIndian Railways to price their product for making them competitive in \nthe International market.  In addition to this , the  Government of India \nextends lines of credit on attractive terms to different countries as a \npart of diplomatic outreach, in cluding the procurement of rail coaches \nfrom India.  Indian Railways, through its marketing arm Rail India \nTechnical and Economic Service (RITES), also participates in \nprocurement tenders for rail coaches as floated in the global market \nfrom time to time. \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|11|UNSTARRED |556", "t": "KVIC Schemes", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 556 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 12.04.2017 \n \n INTRODUCTION OF TRAIN SERVICES \n \n*556. DR. ANUPAM HAZRA: \n \n        Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether there is any legal bar in reintroducing any closed railway \nstoppage of local trains on recently converted broad gauge railway \nline and introducing train service in between one hour gap from \nRampurhat to Howrah under Howrah Division and if so, t he details \nthereof; and  \n \n(b) if not, whether the Railways would consider the proposal for \nreintroducing Nirol Gram Halt station on Ahmadpur -Katwa section and \nintroducing a train service from Rampurhat to Howrah between 4 am \nto 4:30 am from Rampurhat and if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI SURESH PRABHAKAR PRABHU) \n \n(a) & (b):  A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n**** \n \n \n \n \n \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) & (b) OF STARRED \nQUESTION NO. 556 BY DR. ANUPAM HAZRA TO BE ANSWERED IN LOK \nSABHA ON 12.04.2017 REGARDING INTRODUCTION OF TRAIN \nSERVICES. \n \n(a) & (b) As per existing guidelines, Railways may close a halt station \nif it is unremunerative and also not justified on passenger amenity \nground. Railways should a lso consider the closure of halt stations \nwhere average number of passengers is less than 25 per day(outward) \non branch lines and less than 50 per day(outward) on main lines. \nNirolgram halt between Nerol and Panchandi stations over Ahmadpur -\nKatwa section of Howrah Division was closed w.e.f 01.07.2006 due to \nvery poor patronization as the average sale of tickets at Nirolgram \nbefore its closing was only four(04) per day.  At present, gauge \nconversion (NG to BG) in Ahmedpur -Katwa section is under progress \nand restoration of Nirolgram halt is not included in the project \npresently  undergoing gauge conversion. \n \nFurther, at present, Rampurhat and Howrah are connected by 16 pairs \nof Mail/Express and 4 pairs of passenger trains out of which 3 pairs of \ntrains originate/terminate at Rampurhat and Howrah. Out of these, one \nlong distance passenger train viz.  53044 Rajgir -Howrah Passenger \ndeparts Rampurhat at 04.10 Hrs for Howrah. Introduction of any \nadditional trains between 04.00 Hrs to 04.30 Hrs from Rampurhat to \nHowrah is not feasible at present, due to operational and resource \nconstraints. \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|11|UNSTARRED |557", "t": "Weather Forecast for Tourists", "head": "������������������� �\n������������������� �\n�\n��������� �\n������������������������� �\n������������ ���������� �\n�\n����������������������������� �\n�\n����� ����������������������������������� �\n�\n�������������������������������������������������� �\n�\n����� �������� ���� ���������� ��� ������������� ����� �������\n��������������� ����������� ���� ������ �������������\n������������� ���������� ��������� ���� ������ �������� ����������\n��� �������� ������ ���������� ��� ��������� ��������� ������� ��������\n����������������������� �\n����� ������������������������������ ���\n����� ����������������������������� �\n�\n������ �\n�\n�������������������������������������������������� �\n������������������� �\n�\n������������ ������� ��������������� ����������� ������ ���� ���������\n����� ��� � ��������� ������������ ��� ���� �������� ����������� ���������\n�������� ������������� �������� ������������� ������ ���������� �����\n�������� �� ������ ���������� ���� ���������� ���� ����������������\n����������������� �������� ���������� � ����� �������� ���������� ���\n���������������������������������������������������������������������� �\n�\n������� ����� ��� �������� �������� ������� ��� ���� ������\n���������� ��� ������ ��������� ��������������� ����� ������ ����� ������\n��������� �������� ������������� ������ ���������� ������� ��� ������\n����� ���� ����� ������� ��� ����� ����� ������ ��������� ���� ���� �������\n��