8", "t": "Rebate in Luxury and Service Tax", "head": "O.I.H. \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF URBAN DEVELOPMENT \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO 558 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON APRIL 12, 2017 \nTOILET FACILITIES \nNo.  *558   SHRI PANKAJ CHAUDHARY:  \n Will the Minister of URBAN DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n(a) whether the people residing in slum\n unauthorised colonies in urban \nareas are being provided benefits  of Government schemes for \nconstruction of toilets and if so, the details thereof;  \n(b) the details of the funds allocated  and utilised for construction of \ntoilets in slum and unauthorised colonies in urban areas during the \nfinancial years 2015-16 and 2016-17, State-wise; and  \n(c) whether financial assistance ha s been received from foreign \ncountries for construction of toilets in urban areas of the country during \nthe last two years and the current year and if so, the details thereof? \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF URBAN DEVELOPMENT \n(SHRI M. VENKAIAH NAIDU) \n(a) to (c) : A Statement is laid on the Table of the Sabha. \n***** \n\n-2- \n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO. 558 FOR 12.04.2017 REGARDING TOILET FACILITIES \n******* \n(a):   Yes, Madam. Under the Swachh Bharat Mission (Urban) being \nimplemented by the Ministry of Ur ban Development, people residing in \nslum and unauthorised colonies in urban areas are being provided \nbenefits by the Government for construction of individual household \ntoilets (IHHL). Government of India provides Rs  4000 per unit of IHHL to \nthe beneficiaries. Additionally, each state government contributes at \nleast Rs 1333 per unit of IHHL.The Go vernment also provides funds to \nthe Urban local Bodies (ULBs) for constructing Community Toilets (CT), \nfor use by slum residents.  Besides this, Government  also provides funds \nto the ULBs for constructing Public Toilets (PTs) which can be used by \nthe public in general including the residents of the slums and \nunauthorized colonies. The details of IHHLs and CT/PTs constructed \nacross states is given in Annexure 1. \n(b): The state-wise details of funds allocated and released for \nconstruction of toilets is given in Annexure 2. \n (c): No, Madam, no finan cial assistance has been received from foreign \ncountries for construction of toilets in urban areas of the country during \nthe last two years and the current year  \n \n***** \n\n-3- \n \n \n  \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION 558 FOR ANSWER ON 12.04.2017 \nANNEXURE-1 \n \nState-wise details of individual and community/public toilets constructed \nunder SBM (U) \n \nSl. No. State/UT IHHL CT / PT \n1 Andhra Pradesh 349,932 12,176\n2 Andaman & Nicobar Islands 0 0\n3 Arunachal Pradesh 1,056 9\n4 Assam 737 1,988\n5 Bihar 66,680 655\n6 Chandigarh UT 21,999 1,999\n7 Chhattisgarh 243,628 6,239\n8 Daman & Diu 0 0\n9 Dadra & Nagar Haveli 0 0\n10 NCT of Delhi 14 6,862\n11 Goa 914 40\n12 Gujarat 567,003 9,968\n13 Haryana 19,345 1,146\n14 Himachal Pradesh 1,675 30\n15 Jammu & Kashmir 773 510\n16 Jharkhand 112,065 538\n17 Karnataka 122,587 3,232\n18 Kerala 65,976 110\n19 Madhya Pradesh 371,594 15,508\n20 Maharashtra 338,517 3,267\n21 Manipur 236 140\n22 Meghalaya 1 15\n23 Mizoram 2,349 53\n24 Nagaland 3,690 70\n25 Odisha 20,848 967\n26 Puducherry UT 2,277 95\n27 Punjab 27,131 481\n28 Rajasthan 77,533 3,558\n29 Sikkim 1,627 20\n30 Tamil Nadu 296,438 44,290\n31 Telangana 72,550 1,584\n32 Tripura 1 0\n33 Uttar Pradesh 276,728 4,542\n34 Uttarakhand 4,045 339\n35 West Bengal 125,944 161\nTOTAL 3,195,893 1,20,592\n \n\n-4- \n \n \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION 558 FOR ANSWER ON 12.04.2017 \nANNEXURE-2 \n \nState-wise details of funds released during 2015-16 and 2016-17 \n(Rs. in crore) \nSl. No. State/UT IHHL CT \n 2015-16 2016-17 2015-16 2016-17 \n1 A&N Islands 0.02    0.03   \n2 Andhra Pradesh 65.48    3.95   \n3 Arunachal Pradesh 1.21        \n4 Assam   4.00   0.52  \n5 Bihar 20.