���������������������������������������������������������������������������\n���������������� �������������������� ������ �������������������� �������������������� ������ �������������� ���������� �������� ���������������� ������ �������� ���������������� ������\n��������������������������������������������������\n����������\n��\n��\n��"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|11|UNSTARRED |740", "t": "Senior Citizens Welfare Fund", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF SOCIAL JUSTICE AND EMPOWERMENT\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 740\nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07.02.2017\nSENIOR CITIZENS WELFARE FUND\n740. ADV. NARENDRA KESHAV SAWAIKAR:\nWill the Minister of SOCIAL JUSTICE AND EMPOWERMENT be pleased to state:\n(a) whether a senior citizen welfare fund has been established under the Ministry and if so,\nthe details thereof along with the budgetary allocation for the purpose;\n(b) whether act ion plan has been finalised by the Government in this regard and if so, the\ndetails thereof; and\n(c) the manner in which the Government would identify the needy senior citizens and utilise\nthe allocation in rural and urban areas of the country?\nANSWER\nMINISTER OF STATE FOR SOCIAL JUSTICE AND EMPOWERMENT\n(SHRI VIJAY SAMPLA)\n(a): Yes Madam, As per the information provided by Budget Division, Department of Economic\nAffairs, Ministry of Finance, the Central Government has established a Senior Citizens’ Welfar e\nFund (SCWF) which shall be used for such schemes for the promotion of the welfare of Senior\nCitizens. Unclaimed amounts lying in Small Savings Schemes, Employees Provident Fund,\nPublic Provident Fund etc. shall be transferred to the Senior Citizens’ Welf are Fund. As of now\nRs.5889.16 crore has been transferred to this fund.\n(b) & (c): The various Ministries and Departments dealing with matters relating to welfare of the\nSenior Citizens have been requested to forward proposals to the Inter -Ministerial Committee, for\nfunding from the SCWF. The Ministries and Departments while formulating the Schemes are\nexpected to indicate the modalities of identifying the targeted beneficiary Senior Citizens and the\ndetails of utilizing the allocation.\n*****"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|11|UNSTARRED |741", "t": "Traffic Problem in NCR", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.†741  \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 7TH FEBRUARY, 2017 / MAGHA 18, 1938 \n(SAKA) \n \nTRAFFIC PROBLEM IN NCR \n \n†741. SHRI BAHADUR SINGH KOLI: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the Government has the detailed information of places \naffected by traffic jams in the National Capital Region (NCR) particularly \nin Delhi; \n \n(b) if so, the details in this regard and the effective steps being taken to \ncombat this problem; and \n \n(c) whether the Government is considering any solution for improving the \ntraffic arrangements in NCR particularly in Delhi and if so, the details \nthereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI HANSRAJ GANGARAM AHIR) \n \n(a) & (b): The list of areas prone to traffic congestion/jam in the NCT of \nDelhi, as reported by Delhi Police, is at Annexure.    As regard NCR areas \noutside Delhi, the primary responsibility with respect of ‘Police’ & ‘Public \nOrder’ lies with the State Govern ments concerned, as per the Seventh \nSchedule to the Constitution of India. \n.....2/ \n\n \n-2- \nL.S.US.Q.NO. 741 FOR 7.2.2017 \nDelhi Police is constantly engaged in regulation, enforcement and \neducation to road users in the NCT of Delhi with an objective to provide  \nsafe & smooth flow of traffic on Delhi roads.  The steps taken by Delhi \nPolice to combat the problem of traffic congestion/ jam inter -alia include \nprosecution of traffic violators, action against improper parking, action \nagainst motorists driving against the flow of traffic, educating motorists \non road safety through print and mass media, closure of road -cuts to \nensure uninterrupted and smooth flow of traffic and implementing \ntechnology-enabled modernization. \n \n(c): Delhi Police has prepared a Traffic Management Plan to provide \nsafe & smooth flow of traffic on Delhi roads which inter -alia includes \nfocus on traffic regulation, Road Safety education, Engineering Solution \nmeasures & intensive quality enforcement etc.    Delhi Police is provided \nfinancial assistance for modernization of traffic and communication \nnetwork.  \n****** \n  \n  \n\nPAGE 1/1 OF ANNEXURE  \nL.S.US.Q. NO. 741 FOR 07.02.2017 \n \nDetails of areas prone to congestion/traffic jam  \nSl. No. Area Distt. \n1.  ISBT Anand Vihar Eastern Range \n2.  Mukarba Chowk Eastern Range \n3.  G.T.Road Shastri Park Eastern Range \n4.  Akshardham Eastern Range \n5.  Mayur Vihar Metro Station Eastern Range \n6.  Shastri Park Chowk North East Distt. \n7.  Nanaksar towards Yamuna Bridge North East Distt. \n8.  Rohtak Road (Peeragarhi to Mundka) Western Range \n9.  Ring Road (Naraina to Punjabi Bagh) Western Range \n10.  Pankha Road (Kali Mata Mandir to D-Block,Janak Puri) Western Range \n11.  Palam Flyover Western Range \n12.  Uttam Nagar on Najafgarh Road Western Range \n13.  Dwarka Link Road Western Range \n14.  Delhi Gate Najafgarh Western Range \n15.  Chandgi Ram Akhara to Nigam Bodh Ghat North Distt. \n16.  Hanuman Setu to ISBT Kashmiri Gate Ring Road North Distt. \n17.  S.P.M. Marg on both carriageways North Distt. \n18.  Subhash Marg on both carriageways North Distt. \n19.  Rani Jhansi Road North Distt. \n20.  Sadar Bazar North Distt. \n21.  Azad Market North Distt. \n22.  Roshanara Road North Distt. \n23.  Ghanta Ghar on GTK Road North Distt. \n24.  Shakti Nagar North Distt. \n25.  Jawahar Nagar Road from Malka Ganj Chowk North Distt. \n26.  Boulevard Road opposite Tis Hazari North Distt. \n27.  Banglow Road North Distt. \n28.  Kamla Nagar Market North Distt. \n29.  IIT Flyover to Panchsheel Southern Range \n30.  Gurgaon Road – Dhaula Kuan/RR Hospital Southern Range \n31.  Ashram Chowk Southern Range \n32.  Khanpur T- Point Southern Range \n33.  Saket Metro Station Southern Range \n34.  Rao Tula Ram Marg from Moti Bagh Chowk up  Southern Range \n35.  Outer Ring Road Southern Range \n36.  Aurobindo Marg Southern Range \n37.  Mehrauli – Gurgaon Road Southern Range \n38.  Mehrauli – Badarpur Road Southern Range \n39.  Maa Anandmai Marg Southern Range \n40.  Kamal T- Point Central Range \n41.  Asaf Ali Road Central Distt. \n42.  Shradhanand Marg Central Distt. \n43.  In front of NDRS Bhavbhuti Marg Central Distt. \n44.  JLN Marg in front of LNJP Hospital Central Distt. \n45.  Chawari Bazar Central Distt. \n46.  In front of NDRS Chemsford Road Central Distt. \n47.  DBG Road PGC Chowk to NDRS Flyover Central Distt. \n48.  Netaji Subhash Marg Central Distt. \n49.  Military Road to Faiz Road Crossing  Central Distt. \n50.  Entire Karol Bagh Market Area Central Distt. \n51.  Arya Samaj Road Central Distt. \n52.  New Rohtak Road Central Distt. \n53.  Shankar Road Central Distt. \n54.  S-Block Mangol Puri Outer Distt. \n55.  Netaji Subhash Place to Kohat Enclave Outer Distt. \n \n******* "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|11|UNSTARRED |742", "t": "Allotment of DMS Booths", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE & FARMERS WELFARE \nDEPARTMENT OF ANIMAL HUSBANDRY, DAIRYING & FISHERIES \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 742 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 7TH FEBRUARY, 2017 \n \nALLOTMENT OF DMS BOOTHS \n \n742. SHRI DILIP PATEL: \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFAREकृषि और ककसान कल्याण \nमंत्री \n be pleased to state: \n(a)  the criteria adopted by the Government to allot booths by DMS in Delhi;  \n(b) whether the Government is aware that most of the booths are subletted by the original \nallottees; \n(c)  if so, the details thereof;  \n(d)  whether the Government has received complaints in this regard; and  \n(e)  if so, the details thereof and the action taken by the Government thereon along with the \nmanner in which DMS monitors these booths? \n \nA N S W E R \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR AGRICULTURE & FARMERS WELFARE \n(SHRI SUDARSHAN BHAGAT)  \n(a) As per information received from Delhi Milk Scheme (DMS) booths are allotted as per the \nGovernment Policy in order of preference to the eligible applicants who have  applied & \nregistered for allotment of DMS booths in response to the advertisement published in \nnewspapers from time to time. The booth allotment is decided on seniority basis & \npreference is given in following orders:- \n1. Ex-serviceman \n2. War widows \n3. Physical Handicapped \n4. Dependents of deceased DMS employees awaiting appointment on compassionate \ngrounds. \n5. Unemployed persons. \nThe minimum qualification of applicant is 10th pass & minimum age for applying is 18 years and \nmaximum age is not more than 50 years. \n(b) to (e) Yes Madam, Government is aware that DMS had received one complaint of subletting. \nAfter the investigation, the complaint was found true and cancellation of concessionaire ship has \nbeen approved by Competent Authority. Such types of complaints are in vestigated by a team of \nofficers. If complaints are found true, a report is  submitted to the Competent Authority for \ncancellation of concessionaire ship. DMS booths are supervised by the area field officers to \ncheck such type of irregularities. \n***** \n  \n\n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|11|UNSTARRED |743", "t": "Pharma Sector", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF CHEMICALS AND FERTILIZERS \nDEPARTMENT OF PHARMACEUTICALS \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION No. 743 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 7th February, 2017 \n \nPharma Sector \n \n743. SHRI B.V. NAIK: \n \nWill the Minister of CHEMICALS AND FERTILIZERS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government recognizes the pharma sector as a sunshine \nindustry having a tremendous potential for growth and if so, the details \nthereof;  \n \n(b) whether the Government is con sidering to set up a separate Ministry for \npharma and medical devices sector;  \n \n(c) whether the Government is considering to implement the \nrecommendations of the Katoch Committee to cut bulk drugs import from \nChina to help pharma industry in the country; and  \n \n(d) if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND \nHIGHWAYS; MINISTRY OF SHIPPING AND MINISTRY OF CHEMICALS \nAND FERTILIZERS (SHRI MANSUKH L. MANDAVIYA) \n \n(a): Yes, Madam. The Indian Pharmaceutical Industry is witnessing a robust \ngrowth. In the beginning of 11 th Plan in 2007 it stood at approximately Rs. \n71000 crores which has now risen to approximately Rs. 2,00,000 crores as \nper data of Pharmatrac and Pharmexcil upto 2015-16.  \n(b): No, Madam. \n(c) & (d): No f inal view has been taken about implementation of Katoch \nCommittee recommendations yet. \n \nxxxxxx "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|11|UNSTARRED |744", "t": "Warning of DCGI", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF CHEMICALS AND FERTILIZERS \nDEPARTMENT OF PHARMACEUTICALS \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION No. 744 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 7th February, 2017 \n \nWarning of DCGI \n \n744. SHRI SUSHIL KUMAR SINGH: \n \nWill the Minister of CHEMICALS AND FERTILIZERS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Drug Controller General of India (DCGI) has recently issued \nwarning regarding the use of antibiotic medicines amid the news of death of \none person because of its use and h as asked the drug manufacturers to \nissue warning related to its use;  \n \n(b) whether the chemists have also been asked not to supply these \nmedicines without doctor's prescription and if so, the details thereof; and  \n \n(c) the details of the steps taken by the  Government to do away with \ndiscrepancies prevailing in drug industry and medicine shops? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND \nHIGHWAYS; MINISTRY OF SHIPPING AND MINISTRY OF CHEMICALS \nAND FERTILIZERS (SHRI MANSUKH L. MANDAVIYA) \n \n(a) & (b): Drug Controller General of India (DCGI) has informed that they \nhave recently issued a Notice  dated 16.01.2017  to all State/ UT Drugs \nController, Zonal/Sub -Zonal Offices of CDSCO  and Pharma/ Consumer \nAssociations advising them to follow strict r equirements of Schedule H and \nH1 for sale of drugs including antibiotics, which are as follows: \n1. Schedule H: if it contains a substance specified in Schedule H  it is to  be \nlabelled with the symbol Rx and conspicuously displayed on the left top \ncorner of the label and also be labelled with the following words- \nSchedule H drug – warning: To be sold by retail on the prescription of a \nRegistered Medical Practitioner only; \n..2/- \n \n\n \n-2- \n \n2. Schedule H1: if it contains a drug substance specified in Schedule H1, t he \ndrug formulation shall be labelled with the symbol Rx which shall be in red \nand conspicuously displayed on the left top corner of the label, and also be \nlabelled with the following words in a box with a red border- \n“SCHEDULE H1 DRUG – WARNING; \n- It is dangerous to take the preparation except in accordance with the \nmedical advice. \n \n- Not to be sold by retail without the prescription of a Registered Medical \nPractitioner.” \n \n(c): Under Drugs and Cosmetics Act &  Rules, 1945, manufacture for sale, \nand sale for distribution of drugs are regulated by the State Licensing \nAuthority and appointed by the S tate Government. State Licensing Authority \nis empowered to take actions in case of non -compliance with any provision s \nof the said Act and Rules. \n \n \nxxxxxx \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|11|UNSTARRED |745", "t": "Parity of Posts in PSUs", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF SOCIAL JUSTICE AND EMPOWERMENT\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. †745\nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07.02.2017\nPARITY OF POSTS IN PSUs\n†745. SHRI GANESH SINGH:\nWill the Minister of SOCIAL JUSTICE AND EMPOWERMENT be pleased to state:\n(a) the efforts made by the Ministry to establish parity of posts for reserved categories in Public\nSector Undertakings with those in Government offices;\n(b) whether the Ministry has failed to establish parity of posts in these undertakings with those\nin Government offices even after 26 years of implementation of reservation for OBC;\n(c) if so, the reasons therefor;\n(d) whether parity of posts for SC/ST officers/staff working in Public Sector Undertakings has\nbeen established with those in Government offices in the year 1982; and\n(e) if so, the reasons for not implementing it in the case of OBC?\nANSWER\nMINISTER OF STATE FOR SOCIAL JUSTICE AND EMPOWERMENT\n(SHRI KRISHAN PAL GURJAR)\n(a) to (c): No parity has been established between reserved posts in the PSUs with that of Central\nGovernment, since the mode of recruitment, applicable scales of pay and allowances are\ndifferent in the two steams. No such effort is under consideration.\n(d): No, Madam.\n(e): The reservation for OBCs for posts in the Central Government followed the Supreme\nCourt’s judgement dated 15.11.1992 in the Indra Sawhney case (SCC 217).\n*****"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|11|UNSTARRED |746", "t": "Medicinal Plants", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ENVIRONMENT, FOREST AND CLIMATE CHANGE \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION  NO. 746 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07.02.2017 \n \nMedicinal Plants \n \n746. SHRI GODSE HEMANT TUKARAM: \n   \nWill the Minister of ENVIRONMENT, FOREST AND CLIMATE CHANGE be  pleased to \nstate: \n \n(a) whether the Government has any proposal to launch any scheme to protect ancient and \ntraditional medicinal plants and birds in consultation with the State Governments in the \ncountry; \n(b) if so, the details thereof, State-wise including Maharashtra; and \n(c) the details of the steps taken by the Government in this regard including the quantum of \nfunds allocated during the last three years and the current year, State-wise? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) FOR ENVIRONMENT, FOREST AND \nCLIMATE CHANGE  \n(SHRI ANIL MADHAV DAVE) \n \n(a) to (c) The National Medicinal Plants Board, Ministry of AYUSH is implementing a Central \nSector Scheme on Conservation, Development and Sustainable Management of Medicinal \nPlants under which it is providing project based financial assistance to State Governments \n(State Forest Departments & Other agencies etc.) for protection of medicinal plant resources \nthroughout the country, including the State of Maharashtra. Under the scheme, t he in -situ \nconservation of medicinal plants in their natural habitats is being carried out through \ndevelopment of Medicinal Plants Conservation and Development Areas (MPCDAs). During \nthe last three years and current year, a total of Rs. 769.81 Lakh has bee n released to different \nstates for establishment of MPCDAs under above scheme (Annexure I). \n \nFurther, for the protection of birds and their habitats, the Ministry provides financial \nand technical assistance to the State/UT Governments, including the State Government of \nMaharashtra, for Protected Areas and outside Protected Areas under the Centrall y Sponsored \nScheme ‘Integrated Development of Wildlife Habitats’. The State -wise details of funds, \nreleased during the last three years, under this Scheme are given in Annexure - II.  \n***** \n  \n\nAnnexure-II referred to in answer to parts (c) of the Statement in respect of Lok \nSabha Unstarred Question No. 746 due for answer on 07.02.2017 regarding \n“Medicinal Plants”.  \nDetails of release of funds under the Centrally Sponsored Scheme “Integrated \nDevelopment of Wildlife Habitats” during last three years  \n(₹ in lakhs) \nS.No. Name of  \nStates/UTs \n2013-14 2014-15 2015-16 \n \n2016-17 \n(As on \n02.02.2017) \n1 A& N Islands 150.00 00 100.00 118.49 \n2 Andhra Pradesh 00 63.31 0 0 \n3 Arunachal Pradesh 220.439 00 304.02 256.8107 \n4 Assam 138.88 149.11 87.10 0 \n5 Bihar 34.8715 85.249 108.011 100.576 \n6 Chandigarh 0 0 0 26.06514 \n