habad* \n16. Hapur \n17. Shamali \n18.Sambhal \n19. Amethi \n20. Kasganj \n29. Kheri  \n30.Hardoi \n31.Azamgarh \n32.Jaunpur \n33.Badaun  \n34. Sultanpur \n35. Bahraich \n36Moradabad \n37.Gonda \n38.Ghazipur \n39.Rae Bareli  \n40.Muzaffarnagar \n- \n20 \n20 Uttarakhand - - - 3. Pithoragarh \n4. Chamoli \n2 \n21 West Bengal 19.Murshidabad* \n20. Bardhaman* \n- \n41.Paschim \nMedinipur  \n42. Bankura \n43. Jalpaiguri \n44. Birbhum \n- \n6 \nTotal 20 20 44 4 88 \n \n \n\n4 \n \n \nAnnexure-II \n[Part (c) to Lok Sabha USQ No.773 for 07-02-2017] \n \nNumber of existing KVKs considered for upgrading with additional facilities and new \nfacilities during XII Plan. \n \nS.No. Additional facilities No. of KVKs covered \nduring 12th Plan till \nMarch 2017 \n1 Rain Water Harvesting Structure 18 \n2 Soil and Water Testing Laboratory 39 \n3 Minimal Processing Facility  25 \n4 Carp Hatchery 19 \n5 Integrated Farming System units 281 \n6 e-linkag"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|11|UNSTARRED |774", "t": "Mother Dairy and Safal Outlets", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE & FARMERS WELFARE \nDEPARTMENT OF ANIMAL HUSBANDRY, DAIRYING & FISHERIES \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 774 \nTO BE ANSWRED ON 7TH FEBRUARY, 2017 \n \nMOTHER DAIRY AND SAFAL OUTLETS \n \n774. SHRI GUTHA SUKENDER REDDY: \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE  कृषि और ककसान कल्याण मंत्री \n be pleased to state : \n (a)  whether the Government is aware of the problems being faced by Mother Dairy and \nSafal Outlets in the NCT of Delhi, if so, the details thereof; \n(b)  whether it is a fact that the operators/ allottees of Mother Dairy and Safal Booths of \nNCT of Delhi are being given negligible selling margins on the items sold in their outlets that too \n24x7 and 365 days without any holidays;  \n(c)  whether it is a fact that Mother Dairy and Safal supply the inferior quality goods to these \nbooths, if so, the details thereof and the response of the Government thereto;  \n(d)  whether any enquiry has been made by the Government in this regard including the \nliving conditions of the Mother Dairy and Safal booth operators/allottees; and  \n(e) the steps being taken by the Government to rectify the abovementioned irregularities \nfaults and increase the commission being paid to the booth operators? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR AGRICULTURE & FARMERS WELFARE \n(SHRI SUDARSHAN BHAGAT) \n(a) The Government has not received any such reference in respect of NCT of Delhi. \nMother Dairy Fruit &  Vegetable Private Limited (MDFVPL) sells milk and milk products, fruit \nand vegetable in Delhi and NCR through a network of Milk Shops and Safal Fruit & Vegetable \nbooths run by Concessionaires.  \n(b) No, Madam. The margins being provided to Mother Dairy and Saf al booths are  as \nunder:- \n(i) Mother Dairy booths : Average monthly margin paid to a booth Concessionaire is Rs. \n32000/-. Each concessionaire is assured a minimum monthly margin of Rs. 15000/- \n(ii) Safal booths : Average monthly margin paid to a safal booth Concess ionaire is Rs. \n60000/- \n(c) No, Madam. Mother Dairy and Safal  follow good manufacturing practices for \nprocessing, sorting and distributing fresh Fruit & Vegetable products ensuring good quality of \nthe produce as per FSSAI norms. \n(d) No, Madam. \n(e) Does not arise in view of (b) and (d) above.  \n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|11|UNSTARRED |775", "t": "Modern Weapons to Police Force", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 775  \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 7TH FEBRUARY, 2017 / MAGHA 18, 1938 (SAKA) \n \nMODERN WEAPONS TO POLICE FORCE \n \n775.  SHRI BADRUDDIN AJMAL: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether there are reports that the  police personnel do not have \nadequate and  modern weapons to tackle the increasing  terrorist and \nnaxalite activities in the country; \n \n(b) if so, the details ther eof and the  reaction of the Government in this \nregard; \n \n(c) the steps taken by the Government  to equip the police forces with \neffective modern weapons; and \n \n(d) the funds allocated and utilized in  this regard and for modernization of \npolice forces during the last three years? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI HANSRAJ GANGARAM AHIR) \n \n(a)  to (c):   Since  ‘Police’ and ‘Public Order’ are state subjects as per the \nConstitution, r esponsibility of equipping the S tate police forces  with \nappropriate equipment and gadgets lies with the State Governments. \nHowever,   Government   of   India   supplements   the   efforts   of   State  \n.....2/ \n\n-2- \nL.S.US.Q.NO.775 FOR 7.2.2017 \nGovernments by providing central assistance under the Modernisation of \nPolice Forces(MPF) scheme to strengthen police infrastructure. Weaponry is \none of the major items covered under the Scheme and State Governments \nfinalize their annual plans/projects as per their requirements and strategic \npriorities.   A fund is separately allocated to each state for weaponry to be \nsupplied through Ordnance Factory Board. So far as Central Armed Police \nForces are concerned, these Forces are well equipped in terms and arm s \nand ammunitions  as well as other equipments.  \n \n (d):  A statement showing t he total funds earmarked/allocated and \ndisbursed to various States during each of the last three years and the \ncurrent year, state -wise is at Annexure-I.   A statement showing al location \nand release of funds for Megacity Policing, which is a component under MPF \nScheme, is at Annexure-II.  Central Government has incurred expenditure of \nRs. 13.35 crore, 15.47 crore and Rs. 25.83 crore during the years 2014 -15, \n2015-16 and 2016-17 respectively for Arms and Ammunition of CAPFs under \nModernisation Plan-II  \n******** \n  \n\n^ excluding funds for Megacity Policing component and Contingency Reserve of 5%.  \n               # thi