 BVFC- Namrup II 240000.000 16681 11551 69.25% 16681 11551 69.25%   \n\n  Sub-Total  555000.000 14758 9628 65.24% 14758 9628 65.24%   \n                    \n  \nFeed-Stock: \nNaphtha/FO                 \n1 MCFL-Mangalore 379500.000 28845 23715 82.22% 28845 23715 82.22%   \n2 MFL-Madras  486750.000 32049 26919 83.99% 32049 26919 83.99%   \n3 SPIC-Tuticorin 620400.000 30132 25002 82.97% 30132 25002 82.97%   \n  Sub Total 1486650.000 30431 25301 83.14% 30431 25301 83.14%   \n                    \n  Grand Total 20754437.000 19191 14067 73.30% 20250 15125 74.69%   \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|11|UNSTARRED |797", "t": "Foodgrains procured from States", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF CONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD & PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION \nDEPARTMENT OF FOOD AND PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 797 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07th FEBRUARY, 2017 \n \nFOODGRAINS PROCURED FROM STATES \n \n797.  SHRI RAJESHBHAI CHUDASAMA: \nSHRI MALLIKARJUN KHARGE: \n \n \nWill the Minister of CONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD AND PUBLIC \nDISTRIBUTION miHkksDrk ekeys] [kk| vkSj lkoZtfud forj.k ea=h   be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  the quantum of foodgrains procured by the Government from each State \nespecially from Gujarat, year-wise during the last three years; \n \n(b)  whether due to lower procurement  price for foodgrains under MSP \nduring last  two years, the farmers were forced to sell  their produce to private \nagencies and if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c)  whether the Government proposes to increase the MPS for procurement \nat par with the price of foodgrains sold in the  open market so as to provide \nbenefit to the farmers; and \n \n(d)  if so, the details thereof and the action  taken by the Government in this \nregard? \n \nA N S W E R \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR  CONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD & PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION \n(SHRI C. R. CHAUDHARY) \n(a): The State -wise procurement of paddy/rice and wheat for central pool \nduring last three years including Gujarat is enclosed as Annexure -I & II \nrespectively.  \n \n(b): No, Madam. There is a Uniform Policy for procurement by Government \nAgencies across the country. Under this policy, food grains offered by farmers, \nconforming to within stipulated period specifications prescribed are \npurchased at Minimum Support Price (MSP) by the State Government agencies \nincluding Food Corporation of India (FCI) for Central Pool. However, if \nproducer/farmer get better price in comparison to MSP, they are free to sell \ntheir produce in open market i.e. to private tra der/ anyone. The objective of \nprocurement by Government agencies is to ensure that farmers get \nremunerative prices for their produce thereby avoiding distress sale. \n...2/- \n \n\n \n...2... \n \n \n(c) & (d): Government fixes the Minimum Support Prices (MSPs) of various  \nfoodgrains for procurement by Government Agencies based on the \nrecommendation of Commission for Agricultural Costs and Prices (CACP), \nviews of State Governments, concerned Central Ministries and other relevant \nfactors. While formulating its recommendation s on price policy, CACP \nconsiders various important factors that include cost of cultivation, trends in \nmarket prices, demand and supply situation, effect on general price level, \neffect on cost of living etc.  Government of India (GOI) declares MSP for each  \nseason to incentivize the farmers. \n \nThe MSP of Wheat and Paddy in the last 3 years are as follows: \n                                                                        (Rs/Qtl) \n Wheat Paddy \nCommon Grade A \n2014-15 1400 1360 1400 \n2015-16 1450 1410 1450 \n2016-17 1525 1470 1510 \n  \nThe MSP over the past years shows an increasing trend. \n****  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nANNEXURE-I \n \nANNEX REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) OF UNSTARRED QUESTION \nNO