ãâ¨ããè\n \nbe pleased to state:\n \n \n \n(a) \n \nwhether the Government has\n \nrecently discussed with Israeli delegation\n \nfor the \nbilateral cooperation in farm sector\n \nand if so, the details thereof;\n \n \n(b) \n \nwhether Israel has expressed their\n \ncommitment to strengthen bilateral relations\n \nin the field of agriculture and cooperation\n \nin all\nied sectors and if so, the details thereof;\n \n \n(c) \n \nthe level of satisfaction over the\n \nprogress made in cooperation in the\n \nagriculture \nand allied sectors between the\n \ntwo countries; and\n \n \n(d) \n \nthe steps taken by the Government\n \nto further strengthen bilateral r\nelations in\n \nthis \nregard?\n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF  STATE IN THE  MINISTRY OF  AGRICULTURE AND  FARMERS  WELFARE\n \n \n‡ãðŠãäÓã  \nएवं \n\u0000कसान \nक\u0000याण \n½ãâ¨ããÊã¾ã ½ãñâ Àã•¾ã ½ãâ¨ããè          \n \n( SHRI\n \nS.S. \nAHLUWALIA\n \n)  \n \n \n(a)\n \nto (d)\n:\n \nYes, Madam. Since the signing of an Agreement for cooperation in the \nfield of Agriculture on 24.12.1993, the two sides met frequently and held several \ndiscussions. As a result, \nPhase\n-\nI (2010\n-\n2012) and Phase\n-\nII (2012\n-\n2015) of Indo\n-\nIsrael \nAction Plan under t\nhe Agreement have been successfully completed. The two countries \nhave since extended the Action Plan to Phase \n–\n \nIII  for the period 2015\n-\n2018. Under the \nAction Plan, 21 participating States are covered for cooperation in the field of energy \nefficient green\n \nhouses, recycling of waste water for irrigation, Post Harvest Management \nfor horticulture crops, training and visiting facilities in respective countries and private \nsector collaboration.\n \n \n \n \n \n ****  \n\n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|11|UNSTARRED |866", "t": "Illegal Trade between India and Pakistan", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 866 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 7TH  FEBRUARY, 2017/ MAGHA 18, 1938 (SAKA) \n \nILLEGAL TRADE BETWEEN INDIA AND PAKISTAN \n \n866.  SHRI MUTHAMSETTI SRINIVASA RAO (AVANTHI): \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the National Investigation  Agency has come across huge  \nillegal trade between India and Pakistan across the LOC  to fund terrorist \nactivities in Jammu and Kashmir; and \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof and the steps  being taken by the Government \nto check such illegal activities? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI HANSRAJ GANGARAM AHIR) \n \n(a) to (b): The Central Government had received information about illegal \ntransfer of funds from Pakistan to India through import of California \nAlmonds via cross -LOC mechanisms through Trade Facilitation Centers \n(TFC) in Jammu and Kashmir.  Keeping in view the gravity  of the matter \nthe Central Government directed the NIA to take up investigation of this \ncase.  The NIA has registered the case as RC -17/2016/NIA/DLI on \n16.12.2016. \n Three is a well established institutional mechanism to effectively \ndeal with illegal activi ties on the India Pakistan border/Line of Control.  \nThe Unlawful Activities (Prevention) Act, 1967 (UAPA) is an effective \ninstrument to combat offences relating to Terrorist Financing.  A Terror \nFunding and Fake Currency Cell has been set up in the Nationa l \nInvestigation Agency to investigate Terror Funding cases. \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|11|UNSTARRED |867", "t": "Internal Security", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 867 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 7TH  FEBRUARY, 2017/ MAGHA 18, 1938 (SAKA) \n \nINTERNAL SECURITY \n \n867.  DR. SANJAY JAISWAL: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) the details of agencies that are carrying out Research and evelopment \n(R&D) activities pertaining to national security in the country; \n \n(b) the total funds allocated for such  purpose to these agencies during \nthe last three years; \n \n(c) whether the Government has any  proposal to increase the allocation \nfor R&D; and \n \n(d) if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI HANSRAJ GANGARAM AHIR) \n \n \n(a): The Defence Research & Development Organisation (DRDO),  an R& \nD wing of the Ministry of Defence and Bureau of Police Research & \nDevelopment (BPR&D), an organisation under the Ministry of Home \nAffairs, are the two main agencies involved in Research & Development \nactivities for enhancing the operational capabili ties of armed forces and \npolice forces respectively.  \n...2/ \n\n \n \n-2- \nL.S.US.Q.NO 867 FOR 07.02.2017  \n \n \n(b): The total funds allocated in this regard are as under:- \n \n \nYear Modified Appropriation \n(Approved) \n (Rs. in Cr.) \n2013-14 10934.17 \n2014-15 13716.14 \n2015-16 13540.11 \n2016-17 13593.78 (BE) \n            (BE: Budget Estimate) \n \n \n \n(c) & (d): Allocation of funds depends on felt needs of the \nDepartment and overall availability of funds. \n \n \n**** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|11|UNSTARRED |868", "t": "Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE, COOPERATION AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK  SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.\n868\n                      \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE  \n7\nTH\n \nFEBRUARY\n, 2017\n \n \nPRADHAN MANTRI FASAL BIMA \nYOJANA\n \n \n868. \n \nSHRI OM BIRLA:\n           \n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n  \n‡ãðŠãäÓã \nएवं \n\u0000कसान \nक\u0000याण \n½ãâ¨ããè\n \nbe pleased to state:\n \n \n(a) \n \nwhether it is a fact that some farmers\n \norganisations stated that Pradhan Mantri\n \nFasal\n \nBima\n \nYojana does not provide for a universal\n \ncomprehensive coverage of all \ncrops \n \nagainst\n \nall forms of damages and all stages of\n \nthe crop cycle, if so, the details \nthereof;\n \n \n(b) \n \nwhether the Government has\n \nreceived any complaint in this regard, if so,\n \nthe \ndetails of the remedies which\n \nGovernment has initiated to overcome these\n \ndeficits;\n \n \n(c) \n \nwhether the Government has\n \nanalysed the implementation of the\n \nschemes, if so, \nthe number of farmers who\n \nhave benefitted under the scheme along with\n \nthe number of \nState\ns which are doing better\n \nand the ones which have not implemented\n \nthe scheme so \nfar;\n \n \n(d) \n \nwhether the Government has a\n \nproposal to include tenant farmers and\n \nsharecroppers under the scheme who also\n \nbear the risks but do not get any\n \ncompensation, if so, the\n \ndetails thereof; and\n \n \n(e) \n \nwhether the Government has a\n \nproposal to delink insurance from credit\n \nand \nhence making insurance optional, if so,\n \nthe details thereof?\n \n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF  STATE IN THE  MINISTRY OF  AGRICULTURE AND  FARMERS  WELFARE\n \n \n‡ãðŠãäÓã\n  \nएवं \n\u0000कसान \nक\u0000याण \n½ãâ¨ããÊã¾ã ½ãñâ Àã•¾ã ½ãâ¨ããè          \n \n( SHRI \nPARSHOTTAM RUPALA)  \n \n \n(a):\n \nThis Department is not aware of any such statement by any farmers’ \norganizations.  However, Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana\n  \n(PMFBY) provides for \ncomprehensive ri\nsk insurance for all farmers who have availed crop loan and non\n-\nloanee farmers as well for crops/areas notified by the  concerned State Governments.   \nCrop insurance is provided against crop damage from pre\n-\nsowing to post\n-\nharvest losses \nfor food crops (cer\neals, millets and pulses), oilseeds and annual commercial \nhorticultural crops.   The scheme not only safeguards against wide spread yield loss \ndue to non\n-\npreventable natural risks viz.  flood, inundation, landslide, drought, dry \nspells, hailstorm, cyclone,\n \npests/diseases,  natural fire and  lightening, storm, typhoon, \n tempest, hurricane, tornado etc.  but  also against farm level yield loss due to localized risks (hailstorm, landslide and inundation), prevented sowing and post - harvest losses.     \n\n \nContd…2/\n-\n \n \n-\n2\n-\n \n \n(b) \n& (c) : Complaints/suggestions about the scheme are received from various \nquarters from time to time and are looked into in accordance with scheme guidelines \nand insurance principles after consulting all concerned stakeholders.\n \nFurther, the Government continuously monitors and analysis implementation \nrelated issues.   During Kharif 2016, 21 States opted for the scheme, which went up to \n25 States and 3 Union Territories in Rabi 2016.  In Kharif 2016, the coverage in terms \nof numbe\nr of farmers, area and sum insured has exceeded coverage of previous years \nand also the target envisaged for Kharif 2016.  State\n-\nwise provisional details of \ncoverage during Kharif 2016 season are \nannexed\n.  The data clearly demonstrates an \nimproving trend i\nn terms of coverage of farmers, area and sum insured, which is an \noutcome of better and more comprehensive scheme provisions and its  \nimplementation.   Most of the States barring low risk States like Punjab and some \nnorth\n-\neastern States, opted for the sche\nme in 2016\n-\n17.\n \n(d):\n \nPMFBY & RWBCIS already provide for coverage of tenant farmers and \nsharecroppers. \n \n(e):\n \nAt present, no such proposal is under consideration of the Government.\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n  \n\n \n \nAnnexure\n \n \n \nState\n-\nwise provisional details of Farmers Insured, Area Insured and Sum Insured under \nPMFBY during Kharif 2016 season\n \n \n \nSl.\n \nNo.\n \nName\n \nNo. of Farmers \nInsured (Lakhs)\n \nArea Insured \n \n(Lakh Hectare)\n \nSum Insured \n \n(Rs. in Crore)\n \n1.\n \nAndhra Pradesh  \n \n8.54\n \n6.57\n \n5187.84\n \n2.\n \nBihar \n \n14.83\n \n13.11\n \n6526\n \n3.\n \nChhattisgarh\n \n13.26\n \n17.90\n \n6764\n \n4.\n \nGoa\n \n0.007\n \n0.54\n \n5.76\n \n5.\n \nGujarat \n \n11.91\n \n